{{fbdoc item="title" value="FMOD"}}----
Classic FMOD 3.75 audio API using FSOUND and FMUSIC functions.

Website: https://www.fmod.com/core
Platforms supported: ""Win32"", ""Win64"", Linux i386
Headers to include: fmod.bi
Header version: 3.75
Examples: in examples/sound/FMOD/

{{fbdoc item="section" value="SDK and executable architecture"}}
	These examples require the classic 3.75 SDK matching ##fmod.bi##. The publisher's Windows archive contains ##fmod.dll## for i386 and ##fmod64.dll## for x86-64. The archived Linux ##libfmod-3.75.so## is an i386 binary, so a 64-bit Linux PC needs a 32-bit executable and the matching FreeBASIC runtime. Do not mix executable and library architectures.

	Archived publisher downloads are available at https://web.archive.org/web/20060924103009/http://www.fmod.org/files/fmodapi375win.zip and https://web.archive.org/web/20070101000000/http://www.fmod.org/files/fmodapi375linux.tar.gz.

	The binding uses the library name ##fmod##. A GNU import library for Windows x86-64 must refer to ##fmod64.dll## and be available under that link name, for example ##libfmod.dll.a## in a directory selected with ##-p##. On Linux, provide ##libfmod.so## as a link to the genuine versioned SDK library. The original binary remains unchanged.

	The Linux SDK's default output route is OSS. It requires a working ##/dev/dsp## character device, supplied by an OSS driver or a compatible driver such as osspd with its ALSA backend. No-sound initialization can qualify decoding or metadata, but does not demonstrate audio output.

{{fbdoc item="section" value="Examples and metadata ownership"}}
	The module example accepts an optional filename and otherwise uses the bundled module relative to its normal example directory. The two MP3 players require an audio filename argument. Set ##FB_EXAMPLE_AUTOPLAY=1## to perform a bounded playback check without keyboard input. File, playback and cleanup failures return a nonzero exit status.

	Both MP3 players share ##examples/sound/FMOD/fmod_tags.bi##. FMOD returns borrowed metadata byte ranges which remain valid while the stream is open. C ##int## outputs use FreeBASIC ##Long##, including in 64-bit executables. The helper copies text to an owned UTF-8 string, checks each byte boundary, and limits each metadata value to 4 KiB.

	ID3v2 text frames include an encoding byte. The helper supports Latin-1, UTF-16 with a byte-order mark, UTF-16 big endian and UTF-8, returning the first text value. Missing tags, unknown encodings, malformed Unicode and over-budget values yield an empty string. See https://id3.org/id3v2.3.0 and https://id3.org/id3v2.4.0-structure for the text frame definitions.

{{fbdoc item="ex"}}
{{fbdoc item="filename" value="examples/manual/libraries/fmod1.bas"}}%%(freebasic)
'' examples/manual/libraries/fmod1.bas
''
'' Example extracted from the FreeBASIC Manual
'' from topic 'FMOD'
'' Purpose: Play a module with the classic FMOD 3.75 API.
'' Responsibilities: File selection, playback errors and owned module cleanup.
'' This example contains no module decoder or audio driver implementation.
''
'' See Also: https://www.freebasic.net/wiki/wikka.php?wakka=ExtLibfmod
'' --------

#include Once "fmod.bi"

Dim As String sound_file = Command(1)
If sound_file = "" Then sound_file = ExePath() & "/../../sound/data/dne_trtn.mod"

If (FSOUND_GetVersion() < FMOD_VERSION) Then
	Print "FMOD version mismatch"
	End 1
End If

If (FSOUND_Init(44100, 32, 0) = 0) Then
	Print "Could not initialize FMOD: "; FSOUND_GetError()
	End 1
End If

Dim As FMUSIC_MODULE Ptr song = FMUSIC_LoadSong(StrPtr(sound_file))
If (song = 0) Then
	Print "FMOD could not load '" & sound_file & "'"
	FSOUND_Close()
	End 1
End If

If FMUSIC_PlaySong(song) = 0 Then
	Print "Could not start playback: "; FSOUND_GetError()
	FMUSIC_FreeSong(song)
	FSOUND_Close()
	End 1
End If

Dim As Integer playback_error = 0
If Environ("FB_EXAMPLE_AUTOPLAY") = "1" Then
	Sleep 1200, 1
	If FMUSIC_IsPlaying(song) = 0 OrElse FMUSIC_GetTime(song) <= 0 Then playback_error = 1
Else
	Print "Sound playing; waiting for keypress to stop and exit..."
	Sleep
End If

If FMUSIC_IsPlaying(song) Then
	If FMUSIC_StopSong(song) = 0 Then playback_error = 1
End If
If FMUSIC_FreeSong(song) = 0 Then playback_error = 1
FSOUND_Close()
If playback_error Then End 1
Print "FMOD playback completed."

'' end of fmod1.bas
%%

{{fbdoc item="filename" value="examples/manual/libraries/fmod2.bas"}}%%(freebasic)
'' examples/manual/libraries/fmod2.bas
''
'' Example extracted from the FreeBASIC Manual
'' from topic 'FMOD'
'' Purpose: Play an MP3 and read its optional ID3 metadata.
'' Responsibilities: File errors, bounded tag text and owned stream cleanup.
'' This example contains no MPEG decoder or audio driver implementation.
''
'' See Also: https://www.freebasic.net/wiki/wikka.php?wakka=ExtLibfmod
'' --------

'' mp3 player based on FMOD

#include Once "fmod.bi"
#include Once "../../sound/FMOD/fmod_tags.bi"

Dim As String sound_file = Command(1)
If sound_file = "" Then
	Print "Usage: fmod2 <audio-file>"
	End 1
End If

If (FSOUND_GetVersion() < FMOD_VERSION) Then
	Print "FMOD version mismatch"
	End 1
End If
If (FSOUND_Init(44100, 4, 0) = 0) Then
	Print "Could not initialize FMOD: "; FSOUND_GetError()
	End 1
End If
If FSOUND_Stream_SetBufferSize(50) = 0 Then
	FSOUND_Close()
	End 1
End If

Dim As FSOUND_STREAM Ptr fmod_stream = FSOUND_Stream_Open(StrPtr(sound_file), FSOUND_MPEGACCURATE, 0, 0)
If (fmod_stream = 0) Then
	Print "FMOD could not load '" & sound_file & "'"
	FSOUND_Close()
	End 1
End If

'' Copy and decode the borrowed metadata while the stream remains open.
'' An absent or invalid text field yields an empty string.
Print "Title:", get_tag(fmod_stream, "TITLE", "TIT2")
Print "Album:", get_tag(fmod_stream, "ALBUM", "TALB")
Print "Artist:", get_tag(fmod_stream, "ARTIST", "TPE1")
''print_all_tags(fmod_stream)

Dim As Long stream_channel = FSOUND_Stream_Play(FSOUND_FREE, fmod_stream)
If stream_channel < 0 Then
	Print "Could not start playback: "; FSOUND_GetError()
	FSOUND_Stream_Close(fmod_stream)
	FSOUND_Close()
	End 1
End If

Dim As Integer playback_error = 0
If Environ("FB_EXAMPLE_AUTOPLAY") = "1" Then
	Sleep 1200, 1
	If FSOUND_Stream_GetPosition(fmod_stream) = 0 Then playback_error = 1
Else
	Print "Playing MP3, press a key to exit..."
	While Inkey() = ""
		If FSOUND_IsPlaying(stream_channel) = 0 Then Exit While
		Sleep 50, 1
	Wend
End If
If FSOUND_IsPlaying(stream_channel) Then
	If FSOUND_Stream_Stop(fmod_stream) = 0 Then playback_error = 1
End If
If FSOUND_Stream_Close(fmod_stream) = 0 Then playback_error = 1
FSOUND_Close()
If playback_error Then End 1
Print "FMOD playback completed."

'' end of fmod2.bas
%%

